// Tauride Garden data: the AUTHORED ZONES of the garden ground (docs/TAURIDE-REMAKE.md, phase T3). Hand-authored (NOT generated by tools/tauride/build.mjs), pure data: no imports.
// The ground mask (ground-material.js planGroundMask) is computed at start-up from these zones, the relief (height.js), the water outline (data/water.js), the woods (data/footprints.js GARDEN_GREEN, polygons
// from the facade GREEN records), the ways (data/paths.js) and the furniture (data/furniture.js); nothing is stored as a binary. Every number here is a DESIGN value (no survey): it says where the painter put
// mown stripes, worn earth and shade, not where a real lawn is striped.
// Frame: metres from ORIGIN, +X east, +Z south (-Z is north), the frame of the whole project. Rings are flat [x, z, x, z, ...] (not closed).

/** MOWN MEADOWS: the blocks of the open lawn that a gardener mows in bands (the shader draws light and dark stripes of `period` metres across the direction `angle` (degrees, 0 = stripes run east-west, 90 = north-south),
 *  weighted by the openness of the ground: no stripe under a canopy (T5: the planted crowns; the woods and the belt in a mask planned without a planting), on a path, on a steep mound or within 2.5 m of the water). The polygons are
 *  generous on purpose (the crowns cut them back; T5 keeps them open: at most the solitary oaks of data/vegetation.js ZONES.meadow stand on them): the open lawns of the OSM data are the red / green / blue / yellow components of
 *  the T3 plan (D:/git2/n4spb-work/tauride/T3/open-lawn.png), 38,323 m2 of them 3 m inside their edge. At most 7 blocks (the shader table). */
export const MEADOWS = [
  { id: 'sw-lawns',     angle: 14,  period: 3.4, o: [925, -1309, 1211, -1309, 1211, -1595, 925, -1595] },        // the large open lawns of the south-west and the middle (T10 stands here)
  { id: 'se-lobe',      angle: -32, period: 3.6, o: [1325, -1285, 1470, -1285, 1470, -1440, 1325, -1440] },       // the oval lawn between the two arms of the Big pond (the pitch and the sports centre stand on it)
  { id: 'north-lawn',   angle: 78,  period: 3.2, o: [1115, -1620, 1241, -1620, 1241, -1785, 1115, -1785] },       // the open lawn of the north lobe (the north hill N rises in it)
  { id: 'lake-west',    angle: 58,  period: 3.0, o: [1243, -1453, 1324, -1453, 1324, -1593, 1243, -1593] },       // the lawn of the west shore of the Big pond
  { id: 'east-strip',   angle: 90,  period: 3.0, o: [1440, -1440, 1495, -1440, 1495, -1590, 1440, -1590] },       // the strip east of the Big pond (T11 looks at the palace from here)
];

/** THE FALLBACK CANOPY of a mask planned WITHOUT a planting (tools that call planGroundMask alone, the T3 way): the OSM woods (leaf litter) and this belt of old trees along the fence ("old trees at the borders, open lawns in the middle", plan C),
 *  a band of `width` metres inside the outline with the canopy weight `k` (0.30: a shaded-lawn fringe far below the litter threshold of the shader, 0.62 .. 0.78: QA round 1 of T3 found 0.45 + noise tipping it into dark litter blotches), dissolved near gates (`gateClear` m).
 *  T5: the module plants its trees (data/vegetation.js ZONES.belt: the band 1.5 .. 14 m inside the fence, KEEP_OUT.gate 9) and hands the PLANTED CROWNS to the mask (ground-material.js `canopy`): the litter and the shade then lie under the
 *  trees that are there, and this table is not read by the built module. The width was raised 8 -> 12 to match the belt as planted (the aerial: 8-15 m). */
export const CANOPY_BELT = { width: 12, k: 0.30, feather: 4, gateClear: 9 };

/** WORN SPOTS: places that feet and benches wear to bare earth besides the ones the generator finds itself (a bench r 2.6 m, a gate r 5.5 m, a junction of three ways r 2.8 m, a monument or the fountain r 7 m,
 *  the apron of a building 2.6 m): x, z, radius r (m), wear k (0..1; 0.34 .. 0.5 is the first trampled patches, above 0.72 packed earth). */
export const WORN_SPOTS = [
  { id: 'central-round',   x: 1127, z: -1452.3, r: 17, k: 0.9 },    // the great round gravel plaza of the middle of the garden (T7: the user's photo and the satellite: a bare pink-brown disc of ~40 m inside the trees, the low rail fence on it, the benches round it); no furniture node of its own
  // T6: the three plaza spots FOLLOW the furniture data (data/furniture.js FOUNTAINS / MONUMENTS / GATES: `follow` = the OSM node id, dx / dz the hand offset from it; the landmarksTauride.js entry resolves x, z from the node, the x, z written here are what the node gives today and are asserted equal by tools/tauride/furniture-test.mjs)
  { id: 'fountain-plaza',  x: 1282.6, z: -1400.5, follow: 'n950150577', dx: 0, dz: 0, r: 9, k: 0.6 },       // the fountain "Boy with a duck"
  { id: 'south-gate',      x: 1226, z: -1272, follow: 'n828488069', dx: 0, dz: -4.2, r: 9, k: 0.75 },    // the south gate (the people hot spot), 4.2 m inside the fence
  { id: 'memorial-plaza',  x: 1371.2, z: -1451.9, follow: 'n4186236011', dx: 0, dz: 0, r: 9, k: 0.7 },      // the Pioneers memorial
];

/** OSM GREEN records whose polygon is packed earth (playgrounds and the fitness station: the rubber and sand of T6 will cover it); the pitch is NOT listed (its surface is drawn above the ground). */
export const WORN_GREEN_IDS = ['w188083933', 'w69029505', 'w188083935', 'w423708263'];

/** the numbers of the generator (all design values) */
export const GROUND_TUNING = {
  canopyFeather: 6,        // m: the canopy weight goes 0 -> 1 over this distance across the edge of a wood (0.5 at the edge: the litter territory starts at the edge)
  shoreBand: 3,            // m: the width of the muddy shore band that the shader draws (the relief keeps the 3 m beside the water flat for T4)
  benchR: 2.6, benchK: 0.8,
  gateR: 5.5, gateK: 0.9,
  junctionR: 2.8, junctionK: 0.62,
  monumentR: 7, monumentK: 0.75,
  apron: 2.6, apronK: 0.6,
  verge: 1.2, vergeK: 0.30,     // the worn edge of a path: wear 0.30 at the path edge, 0 at 1.2 m (QA round 1 of T3: 0.36 stained the verges)
  stripeFeather: 3,        // m: the stripe weight of a block goes 0 -> 1 over this distance inside its edge
  shoreClear: 2.5,         // m: no stripes this close to the water
};
